<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Nurmekund</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Estonian district in the centre of the country, mentioned in Henry of Livonia's chronicle and conquered in the 1220s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Nurmekund, called Normegunde in the sources, was a minor Estonian land in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sakala">Sakala</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jarvamaa">Järvamaa</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alempois">Alempois</a>. It is known only from brief mentions in the chronicle of the Livonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It was probably a union of a few parishes under elders, sharing the customs and pagan religion of the larger Estonian counties around it. No leaders or details of its organisation are recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Nurmekund was subdued during the conquest of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>, completed in 1224, and passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nurmekund.jpg" alt="Nurmekund" width="320" height="219"><figcaption>Image: 藏骨集团 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Estonian_counties.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Normegunde</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=nurmekund" aria-label="Nurmekund on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5226 201 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nurmekund lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5546 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5546 457h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=nurmekund">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

